{
  "_about": "v79.8 (Block B): the norms that confer an action. A claim candidate («Fondare la domanda sull'art. X», a riconvenzionale) is built only on an article one of these rules admits: an institution module's «actions» (the institution the first read names, or the case's words: «patterns») or a remedies.json matter's «actions». A module's articles come first, in its order (the specific norm before the general one: 2053 before 2051); «general» (1218, 1453, 2043) are subordinate -- offered with a module only when the module yields nothing proven. «limiting» are never a claim (they measure or condition a claim, they confer none). Edit here; lawyer_method.claim_admission reads it. v79.8.5: modules marked «draft» are Code's proposal, for the lawyer's review (famiglia, consumo, lavoro beyond the licenziamento, successioni, condominio). v79.9 (Block B): a module may carry «stages» (the stage its articles differ by, read from the case's certain facts -- «patterns» -- or the events the terms read -- «events»: consegna, fine lavori, scoperta vizio, denuncia/reclamo; the first stage that matches puts its «actions» first), «conditional» actions (offered only when a certain fact matches their patterns: 1439 on a false description), «non_actions» (code articles that are no claim norm for the client: 2118, 2119 for a dismissed worker), «laws» (the special laws that govern it, checked against the graph's primary documents: data/corpus_expected.json holds the same list, with how each is matched), «requires» («professional_counterparty»: the consumer module only with a business as a certain fact) and «name».",
